1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:01,501
In this video, I'm going to

2
00:00:01,501 --> 00:00:04,604
walk you through how to use the 3D
printed Braille Embosser.

3
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:08,641
You want to start by aligning
the indicator triangles.

4
00:00:09,042 --> 00:00:09,876
Turn the handle

5
00:00:09,876 --> 00:00:13,613
until the triangles on both cylinders
are directly on top of each other.

6
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:17,183
This is what the starting position
should look like.

7
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:19,686
Once the triangles are aligned
and in the starting

8
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:22,689
position, rotate
the entire Braille Embosser.

9
00:00:22,789 --> 00:00:25,191
so the rollers are horizontal.

10
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:28,561
To line up the embossed Braille dots
with the printed information

11
00:00:28,561 --> 00:00:31,631
on your business card,
use the indicator triangles as your guide.

12
00:00:31,798 --> 00:00:34,167
The triangles are pointing
in the up direction,

13
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:37,170
to show you which way
the Braille is going to be embossed.

14
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:41,207
You then orient your card
to make sure that it rolls from left

15
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:42,909
to right, with the printed information

16
00:00:42,909 --> 00:00:45,912
facing up in the directions
that the triangles are pointing.

17
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:49,549
I find it helpful to use gravity to level
the card.

18
00:00:49,582 --> 00:00:52,419
I do this by dropping it into place
between the rollers.

19
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:54,154
and double checking that it seems level.

20
00:00:56,189 --> 00:00:56,856
Next,

21
00:00:56,856 --> 00:00:59,859
rotate the handle forward
about a half turn.

22
00:00:59,859 --> 00:01:03,196
Another technique I found helpful
is to flip the embosser partway through

23
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:06,266
so I can watch the dots forming
and make sure that they all look good.

24
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:09,502
By going back and forth a few times,
you can make sure that every dot

25
00:01:09,502 --> 00:01:10,637
is fully embossed.

26
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:14,707
This only works really well if you're able
to stop before going over the last dot.

27
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:17,911
If you go too far
you may get a misaligned print.

28
00:01:18,711 --> 00:01:20,780
Once all the dots look correctly embossed,

29
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:23,783
you can go ahead and roll it
all the way through.

30
00:01:25,151 --> 00:01:28,154
And that's it.

31
00:01:28,488 --> 00:01:30,223
A quick note on settings:

32
00:01:30,223 --> 00:01:34,027
This embosser is the 0.4mm
cardstock setting.

33
00:01:34,194 --> 00:01:37,797
If you have thinner business cards,
make sure you use the 0.3mm

34
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:39,466
cylinder preset instead.

35
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:44,037
If at any point you want to change out
the cylinders,

36
00:01:44,037 --> 00:01:47,040
you can just pull the lid off
and let the handle stay attached.

37
00:01:47,574 --> 00:01:51,144
Sometimes new rollers can get
stuck into the base, and if that happens,

38
00:01:51,377 --> 00:01:54,314
I recommend using a small flathead
screwdriver

39
00:01:54,314 --> 00:01:57,283
help work them loose.

40
00:01:57,383 --> 00:02:01,454
And that's how you operate and swap
cylinders on the 3D printed Braille

41
00:02:01,454 --> 00:02:02,789
Embosser.

42
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:05,892
If you run into any issues
or want to contribute to the project,

43
00:02:06,192 --> 00:02:09,162
the GitHub link is in the app
and in the video description.
